              "text": "год (god) from Proto-Slavic godŭ, \"a fitting time, a season\" — inherited; Old Russian godŭ meant \"time, term\" (Vasmer). Vasmer relates it to Latvian gadīgs, \"capable\", and Old High German gigat, \"fitting\"; the same root is in годиться, \"to be fit\"."
